# Allowlist for tools/check-orphans.sh
# Every entry must have a # REASON — an unjustified entry defeats the check.
#
# The gate flags files whose only production importers are inside the same
# directory (barrel, sibling files). These entries exempt files that are
# transitively reachable through their feature barrel → external consumer.
# Each entry documents the chain: Filename ← barrel ← external_consumer.

# ── apps/api ──

# FcmPushTransport is wired through the PUSH_TRANSPORT DI token via
# useExisting in push.module.ts. The class name is never directly
# referenced outside its module, but NestJS injects it through the
# token system. It is not orphaned — it is the push transport.
api:FcmPushTransport

